      "writtenOn": "2026-04-21T17:13:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Strict Aliasing Violation (`bootrom.cc`)** In `send_bootrom_command_aes`:\n\n```c\nuint32_t rsp_wrapped_len \u003d *reinterpret_cast\u003cconst uint32_t *\u003e(\u0026ret[2]);\n```\n\n* **Risk:** Casting a byte array pointer to a `uint32_t` pointer and dereferencing it violates C++ strict aliasing rules and can lead to Undefined Behavior (UB), particularly on ARM architectures where unaligned memory access might cause faults.  \n* **Remediation:** Use `std::memcpy` to safely extract the value:\n\n```c\nuint32_t rsp_wrapped_len;\nstd::memcpy(\u0026rsp_wrapped_len, \u0026ret[2], sizeof(rsp_wrapped_len));\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 179,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 180,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "02e7aba6221e427ee896ab011f1564dc64af6f53",
