      "writtenOn": "2026-04-21T17:13:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**. Magic Numbers vs. Defined Constants (`bootrom.cc`)** You have excellently defined command constants in `EgisBootrom` namespace within `bootrom.h` (e.g., `CMD_MEM_READ \u003d 0x20`), but you frequently fall back to magic numbers in the implementation:\n\n* In `backup_flash`: `data.push_back(0x20);` \\-\\\u003e Should be `EgisBootrom::CMD_MEM_READ`.  \n* In `get_otp_info`: `0x23` \\-\\\u003e Should be `EgisBootrom::CMD_OTP_READ`.  \n* **Remediation:** Replace all instances of `0x20`, `0x21`, `0x22`, and `0x23` in array initializations with their respective enum/namespace constants.",
