      "side": 1,
      "message": "**. Hex String Parsing Vulnerability (`et171_flash.cc`)** When parsing `-offset` and `-size` using `strtoul`:\n\n* **Risk:** If a user provides a negative number (e.g., `-offset -100`), `strtoul` will silently underflow and wrap around to a massive positive number, which will likely crash the flash loop.  \n* **Remediation:** Parse the string as a signed integer using `strtol` first, verify it is `\u003e 0`, and then cast to `uint32_t`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "02e7aba6221e427ee896ab011f1564dc64af6f53",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
